Make the macOS browser process's Cocoa language and region follow --lang (in
memory only, through the NSUserDefaults argument domain), so strings macOS
localizes itself -- speech voice names and the language names Chrome appends
to duplicate voice names -- match the requested language instead of the host's.
With --lang, the default speech voice is the system default for that language
rather than the host's Spoken Content selection. Without --lang, or with a
value that does not look like a language tag, behaviour is unchanged.

